317
00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:33.550
I just love it.
我太喜欢了。

318
00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:38.010
I loved Kate strapped to Brian's back, but we'll get to that.
我很喜欢凯特被绑在布莱恩背上的样子，但我们待会儿再说这个。

319
00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:38.370
Okay.
好的。

320
00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:44.310
Well, Danny Chun said the writers got the idea to do an office Lip Dub back in April or May
丹尼·春说，编剧们是在四五月份的时候想出要拍一个办公室“对口型”视频的，

321
00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.830
before the summer break, before the end of season six.
在暑假前，也就是第六季结束之前。

322
00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:52.570
He said they'd been just watching Lip Dubs like we all were, but he thought,
他说他们当时也像我们大家一样在看各种“对口型”视频，但他想，

323
00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:56.270
but what I'd love to see is one that's kind of full of mistakes.
他想看一个充满失误的版本。

324
00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:56.910
Yeah.
是啊。

325
00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:00.010
And he said that felt like a fun idea to play with.
他说这听起来是个很有趣的创意。

326
00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:04.010
But Danny said they kind of forgot about the idea for a while, but when it came time to
但丹尼说他们把这个想法搁置了一段时间，不过当到了

327
00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:06.350
pitch on the season premiere, Danny brought it up again.
构思季首播集的时候，丹尼又提了出来。

328
00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:11.710
On the DVD commentary, Danny said that this cold open Lip Dub was one of the most fun things
在DVD评论音轨里，丹尼说这个开场“对口型”视频是他参与过的

329
00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.130
he's ever been a part of.
最有趣的事情之一。

330
00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:17.830
He said he wrote it in one day, and it was originally supposed to start in the parking
他说他花了一天时间写完剧本，原本计划是从停车场开始，

331
00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.270
lot.
然后穿过仓库，最后进入办公室。

332
00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:21.550
And then it was going to come through the warehouse and end up in the office.
但正如你所知，珍娜，现实中这些建筑并不相连，所以他们

333
00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:26.550
But since none of those buildings are connected in real life, as you know, Jenna, they could
无法一镜到底。

334
00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.570
not do it in one take.
因此我们的导演杰夫·布里茨建议全部在主办公室拍摄，这样我们

335
00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:32.830
So our director, Jeff Blitz, suggested it all take place in the main office so that we
就能实现那种一镜到底的效果。

336
00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.090
could do that whole one take look.
这就引出了我们的下一个问题：你们拍了多少次？

337
00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:40.650
That leads me into our next question, which was, how many takes did you have to do?
真的是一镜到底，还是用了什么剪辑技巧？

338
00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:45.030
And was it really one take or was there some sneaky editing involved?
伙计们，这取决于你问谁。

339
00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:49.370
Well, guys, this kind of depends on who you ask.
这很有趣。

340
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.750
This was very funny.
每个人的记忆在这件事上都有点出入。

341
00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:54.010
Everyone's memory was a little different on this one.
根据丹尼·春的说法，这是一个长镜头，我们大概拍了三四次。

342
00:14:54.210 --> 00:15:00.650
According to Danny Chun, it was one long continuous take, and we did it about three or four times.
我的记忆是这是一个长镜头，我记得我们拍了三次。

343
00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:08.130
My memory was that it was one long take, and I remembered that we did three.
安吉拉，你记得是什么样的？

344
00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:10.270
Angela, what did you remember?
我也记得这是一个长镜头，因为这是一个多米诺骨牌效应，

345
00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:15.310
I remembered that it was all one long take as well, because it was a domino effect of
一环扣一环。

346
00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:15.610
things.
当时我在达里尔的办公室里，我得关上门。

347
00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:19.190
So I was there in Daryl's office, and I had to shut the door.
但我关门的动作是给安迪的信号，让他喊“快，快，快”。

348
00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.930
But me shutting the door cued Andy to say, go, go, go.
所以我只记得所有这些瞬间，我们确实是一镜到底拍完的。

349
00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:27.710
So I just remember all of these moments, and we did it all in one take.
但我确实记得我们很快就搞定了。

350
00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.790
But I do remember that we got it pretty quickly.
但我确实记得我们很快就搞定了。

351
00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.890
Like, we were impressed with ourselves.
我们当时对自己印象深刻。

352
00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.650
We were like, oh my gosh, we got that.
我们当时心想，天哪，我们竟然做到了。

353
00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:35.870
Yeah, same memory.
没错，记忆是一样的。

354
00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:41.130
Well, when we reached out to cinematographer Matt Stone, he confirmed that we did do this
嗯，当我们联系摄影指导马特·斯通时，他证实我们确实是这样做的，

355
00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:43.150
as one long continuous take.
作为一个长镜头拍摄。

356
00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:49.710
However, he said that they did work in a couple of spots where we could cut if we needed to,
不过，他说他们确实预留了几个可以剪辑的地方，以备不时之需，

357
00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:52.990
but we did shoot it as one long take.
但我们确实是把它当作一个长镜头来拍的。

358
00:15:54.010 --> 00:16:00.250
So then, when we reached out to our editor, Dave Rogers, he actually went back and checked
所以，当我们联系我们的剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯时，他回去查了查

359
00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:00.930
his files.
他的文件。

360
00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:03.750
He said we did five takes.
他说我们一共拍了五条。

361
00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.590
And he sent them to us.
他还把这些素材发给了我们。

362
00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:06.590
Amazing.
太棒了。

363
00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:11.870
He said we used a combination of take four and take five.
他说我们用了第四条和第五条的组合。

364
00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:20.010
So he said it's mostly all take five, but we cut when Angela slams Daryl's office door,
所以他说大部分都是第五条，但在安吉拉猛关达里尔办公室门的时候我们剪辑了一下，

365
00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:26.950
and then we cut on the whip to take four as the camera moves by Phyllis dancing and heads
然后镜头扫过菲利斯跳舞时切换到第四条，接着镜头移向

366
00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.390
into Michael's office as he performs the magic tricks with his wand.
迈克尔的办公室，他在那里用魔杖表演魔术。

367
00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:35.330
And then we whip out back to take five as Andy yells, streamers.
然后当安迪大喊“彩带”时，我们又切回了第五条。

368
00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:38.070
And then we stayed in take five until the end.
之后我们就一直保持在第五条直到结束。

369
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:43.510
And Dave said, looking at all the takes, he thinks the reason we did this was because
戴夫说，查看了所有拍摄素材后，他认为我们这样做的原因是因为

370
00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:50.630
Steve's magic in his office was best in take four, and they really wanted that magic take
史蒂夫在办公室里的魔术表演在第四条中表现最好，他们非常想把那段魔术

371
00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.050
in the episode.
放进剧集里。

372
00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:57.650
I just have to give a big thank you to Dave Rogers because we all had different memories,
我必须向戴夫·罗杰斯表示衷心的感谢，因为我们大家的记忆各不相同，

373
00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:00.070
and he had the answer.
而他给出了答案。

374
00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.230
Yeah, thank you, Dave.
没错，谢谢你，戴夫。

375
00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:07.050
Incidentally, in terms of Michael's magic, Danny Chun shared that they basically just
顺便提一下，关于迈克尔的魔术，丹尼·春分享说，他们基本上只是

376
00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:11.170
gave Steve a bunch of dorky magic tricks and let Steve improvise it.
给了史蒂夫一堆笨拙的魔术道具，然后让史蒂夫即兴发挥。

377
00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:16.590
So each of those magic takes in his office were a little bit different, except for the fire
所以他在办公室里的每一段魔术表演都略有不同，除了火焰

378
00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:17.010
part.
那部分。

379
00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:20.770
Yeah, they had a magician's helper named Amos Levkovich.
是的，他们请了一位魔术师助手，名叫阿莫斯·列夫科维奇。

380
00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:25.410
He was hiding behind Michael's door to preset that flame trick at the end.
他躲在迈克尔的门后，为最后那个火焰魔术做准备。

381
00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.890
So here were all of Michael's tricks.
所以这就是迈克尔所有的魔术。

382
00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:33.470
A dove comes out of his wand, flowers appear out of his cane, and then, of course, that
鸽子从魔杖里飞出来，花从手杖里变出来，当然，还有最后

383
00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:34.670
flame in his hand.
他手里的那团火焰。

384
00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:40.930
And I remember Steve loved that dove coming out of the wand, and he does it like three
我记得史蒂夫很喜欢鸽子从魔杖里飞出来那个桥段，他大概做了

385
00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.490
times.
三次。

386
00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:42.070
I know.
我知道。

387
00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.190
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

388
00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:44.830
All right, let's see.
好了，让我们看看。

389
00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.070
Next question, how did they choose which song to use?
下一个问题，他们是如何选择使用哪首歌的？

390
00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.030
Well, that was all Danny.
嗯，那全是丹尼的主意。

391
00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.470
It was the only song he considered.
那是他唯一考虑过的歌。

392
00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:58.390
He said he really wanted a song that was, quote, short, upbeat, fun to lip sync to, and
他说他真的很想要一首“短小、欢快、适合对口型，而且

393
00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.430
not too current.
不太过时”的歌。

394
00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:04.170
Randy said it cost us $50,000 to get the song rights.
兰迪说我们花了五万美元才买下这首歌的版权。

395
00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:08.370
And we should probably add that we could really hear that song.
我们或许应该补充一点，我们当时真的能听到那首歌。

396
00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:12.910
They had speakers, like, hidden all around the set, and it was really playing the song.
他们在片场各处都藏了扬声器，真的在播放那首歌。

397
00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.870
We were really doing, like, lip syncing.
我们当时确实是在对口型。

398
00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:15.230
Yeah.
没错。

399
00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:19.730
And I mean, I don't think you can fake that kind of energy that a song brings.
我的意思是，我不认为你能伪造出那种音乐带来的活力。

400
00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:22.730
I was so glad that they were playing it throughout the office.
我很高兴他们当时在整个办公室里播放着这首歌。

401
00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:23.230
Yes.
是的。

402
00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:29.070
Our next questions are, who came up with the choreography, and what was the rehearsal process
接下来的问题是，谁负责编舞，

403
00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:29.490
like?
排练过程又是怎样的？

404
00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.450
This was heavily choreographed, you guys.
伙计们，这段舞是经过精心编排的。

405
00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

406
00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:37.030
So, the lip dub was choreographed by Mary Ann Kellogg.
所以，这段对口型表演是由玛丽·安·凯洛格编排的。

407
00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.410
She planned it out with a team of dancers.
她和一支舞者团队一起策划了整个过程。

408
00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:44.390
They shared on the DVD commentary that every single detail you see was planned.
他们在DVD评论音轨里分享说，你们看到的每一个细节都是提前规划好的。

409
00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.570
Randy Cordray even sent us their rehearsal video.
兰迪·科德雷甚至把他们的排练视频发给了我们。

410
00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:49.870
I loved watching it, Jenna.
我超爱看那个视频，珍娜。

411
00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:50.450
Me too.
我也是。

412
00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.190
They had all these dancers doing our part.
他们找了所有这些舞者来替我们排练。

413
00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.170
Way better than we did them, by the way.
顺便说一句，他们跳得比我们好多了。

414
00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:55.370
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

415
00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:56.250
Like, real dancers.
毕竟是专业的舞者。

416
00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:57.710
They were amazing.
他们太棒了。

417
00:18:57.910 --> 00:18:59.930
The rehearsal dancers need a shout-out.
这些排练舞者值得被特别鸣谢。

418
00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:06.330
They were Tammy Toe, Lauren Marie Menendez, Michael Cothran Penna, Jennifer Mimi Karsh,
他们分别是塔米·托、劳伦·玛丽·梅嫩德斯、迈克尔·科特兰·彭纳、詹妮弗·米米·卡什、

419
00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.250
Aaron Cash, and John Todd.
亚伦·卡什和约翰·托德。

420
00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.750
They were so great.
他们真的太出色了。

421
00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.350
We couldn't have done this without them.
没有他们我们根本完成不了。

422
00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:16.330
Randy Cordray said, we can put the rehearsal in our Insta stories so you guys can watch it.
兰迪·科德雷说，我们可以把排练视频发到我们的Instagram快拍上，这样你们就能看到了。

423
00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:21.330
And Danny said they had scripted out all the beats, but there were little things that were tricky.
丹尼说他们把所有的节奏点都写进了剧本，但有些小细节处理起来很棘手。

424
00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:25.510
For example, getting Aaron from reception to the kitchen in time,
比如，要及时让亚伦从前台赶到厨房，

425
00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:31.170
or the fact that he wrote in the script that Meredith is strapped to Kevin's back in the break room.
或者剧本里写着梅雷迪思要背在凯文背上出现在休息室。

426
00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:31.430
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

427
00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.690
He just wrote that down.
他随手就写下了这一条。

428
00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:33.030
Yeah.
是啊。

429
00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.490
But how to make that happen.
但要怎么实现呢？

430
00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:35.190
Exactly.
确实。

431
00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:39.310
Kelly Cantley shared that our special effects coordinator, Mike Thompson,
凯莉·坎特利分享说，我们的特效协调员迈克·汤普森，

432
00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:41.910
built the harness that Kate had to wear.
制作了凯特必须穿戴的背带装置。

433
00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:45.070
And you guys, I reached out to Kate because I was like,
伙计们，我联系了凯特，因为我当时想，

434
00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:48.310
Kate, will you please tell me about being strapped to Brian's back?
凯特，你能跟我说说被绑在布莱恩背上是什么感觉吗？

435
00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:49.390
How did you do it?
你是怎么做到的？

436
00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:50.290
What was the process?
过程是怎样的？

437
00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:51.810
Here's what she had to say.
来看看她是怎么说的。

438
00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.990
Hey, it's Kate Flannery.
嘿，我是凯特·弗兰纳里。

439
00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:56.530
Okay, so this is the deal.
好的，情况是这样的。

440
00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:00.370
I was on a harness on Brian's back.
我当时被绑在布莱恩背上的背带里。

441
00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:07.010
There was a table behind us so that I wasn't putting all my weight on him the entire time.
我们身后有一张桌子，所以我不用一直把全身重量都压在他身上。

442
00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.290
So I would squat on the table, even though it was high up,
所以我蹲在桌子上，尽管位置很高，

443
00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:12.810
just to get my weight off of his back.
只是为了减轻他背上的负担。

444
00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:14.490
Like, don't break another actor.
毕竟，不能把另一位演员压垮了。

445
00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:15.210
Don't do it.
千万别那么做。

446
00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:21.270
Anyway, so I'm on his back on this crazy harness,
总之，我穿着这个疯狂的背带在他背上，

447
00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.370
and then he turns around,
然后他转过身，

448
00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:29.130
and I have the word nobody on my stomach.
我的肚子上写着“没人”这个词。

449
00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:31.870
Okay, the first time we do it, it's perfect.
好吧，我们第一次尝试就非常完美。

450
00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:33.910
The whole thing was perfect.
整个过程简直完美无缺。

451
00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:36.650
Like, you guys, there's no cut in a lip dub.
伙计们，唇语同步视频是不能剪辑的。

452
00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.290
It has to be all one take.
必须一镜到底。

453
00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.510
So everybody has to get their part right.
所以每个人都得把自己的部分演好。

454
00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:40.890
Everybody.
每个人。

455
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:41.630
And we did.
我们确实做到了。

456
00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:47.730
Except that they felt like my nobody was too faded.
除了他们觉得我身上的“nobody”字样太淡了。

457
00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.710
The marker had, like, absorbed into my skin.
记号笔的墨水好像渗进我的皮肤里了。

458
00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:53.290
So I feel like I let everybody down.
所以我感觉我让大家失望了。

459
00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.090
So we had to do, we did,
所以我们不得不，我们确实，

460
00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.910
I think we did two more takes for safety,
我想我们为了保险起见又拍了两次，

461
00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.090
but I still feel like we would have had it on the first one
但我还是觉得如果能看清我身上的“nobody”，

462
00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:00.270
if you could read my nobody.
我们第一次就成功了。

463
00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:04.190
So my pasty white skin absorbed the Sharpie.
我那苍白的皮肤把记号笔的墨水给吸收了。

464
00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.970
It was, yeah, it took a couple days for it to come off.
确实，过了好几天才洗掉。

465
00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:09.810
I'll be honest with you.
说实话。

466
00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.630
It's kind of weird to look in the mirror
照镜子的时候感觉挺奇怪的，

467
00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:16.210
when you're taking a shower or getting dressed,
尤其是在洗澡或穿衣服的时候，

468
00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.270
and your stomach says nobody.
肚子上写着“nobody”。

469
00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:20.870
Ugh, don't try this at home, folks.
呃，大家在家里可别尝试这个。

470
00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.110
But she said that nobody,
但她说那个“nobody”，

471
00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.250
they had to go back and ride it over
他们不得不回去重新描一遍，

472
00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.210
and, you know, really darken it.
你知道，把它加深。

473
00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.370
And it was there for days.
结果它在身上留了好几天。

474
00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.130
Well, I loved this day.
嗯，我很喜欢那天。

475
00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.930
I remember we came in early and we rehearsed,
我记得我们很早就到了，先进行了排练，

476
00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.890
and then we went to hair and makeup.
然后去了化妆间。

477
00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.130
And I remember Randy told us we had the whole day.
我记得兰迪告诉我们那天全天的时间都归我们。

478
00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:43.090
We should just take the day.
我们可以慢慢来。

479
00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:44.150
Right, no stress.
对，没压力。

480
00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:45.930
Yeah, and all the dancers were there.
是啊，所有的舞者都在那儿。

481
00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:50.010
We watched their video, and then whoever was dancing our part
我们看了他们的视频，然后负责跳我们那部分的舞者

482
00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.370
would show us our part.
会教我们动作。

483
00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:52.490
And show us the timing.
还会教我们节奏。

484
00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:53.870
Mm-hmm, yes.
嗯，没错。

485
00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:55.710
So Randy told me that, yes,
所以兰迪告诉我，是的，

486
00:21:55.850 --> 00:21:57.850
we started rehearsing at 7.15 in the morning.
我们早上7点15分开始排练。

487
00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:00.610
We got our first take at 11.23.
我们在11点23分完成了第一次拍摄。

488
00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:03.670
That's the precision of Randy Cordray.
这就是兰迪·科德雷的精准度。

489
00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:05.090
He knows the exact moment.
他知道确切的时间点。

490
00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:07.110
He's like an air traffic controller.
他就像个空中交通管制员。

491
00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:08.910
Your flight will leave at 7.12.
你的航班将在7点12分起飞。

492
00:22:09.170 --> 00:22:10.070
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

493
00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.430
Okay, all right, Randy.
好吧，行，兰迪。

494
00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:14.650
And we wrapped for the day at 1.36.
我们下午1点36分就收工了。

495
00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:16.570
6, and it was just so much fun.
6分，那真是太有趣了。

496
00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:18.770
That's an early wrap day for us, you guys.
伙计们，这对我们来说可是个早收工的日子。

497
00:22:18.890 --> 00:22:20.210
So that meant we had the whole afternoon.
这意味着我们整个下午都有空。

498
00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:21.430
We were probably so excited.
我们当时一定特别兴奋。

499
00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:22.110
I know.
我知道。

500
00:22:22.390 --> 00:22:25.170
I remember our biggest hurdle was that there was a big cleanup
我记得我们最大的障碍是当时有一场大清理

501
00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:26.490
between each take.
在每次拍摄间隙。

502
00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:27.050
Right, the confetti.
对，还有五彩纸屑。

503
00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:28.730
With all the streamers and everything.
还有所有的彩带之类的东西。

504
00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:32.150
But besides that, we were able to really go through those takes
但除此之外，我们确实能很快地

505
00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:32.830
pretty quickly.
完成那些拍摄。

506
00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:35.230
Angela, I got a fan question.
安吉拉，我有个粉丝提问。

507
00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:35.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

508
00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:40.870
From Ian Oh in South Africa and Diana T in Paris, France
来自南非的伊恩·欧和法国巴黎的戴安娜·T

509
00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:45.870
to international folks who are wondering,
问了一些国际粉丝想知道的问题，

510
00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:49.250
Angela, were you bummed that you couldn't really participate
安吉拉，你没能真正参与

511
00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:52.150
in the Lip Dub festivities?
“对嘴演唱”活动，你会感到沮丧吗？

512
00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:54.270
I mean, you know me in real life.
我是说，你在现实生活中了解我。

513
00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:56.050
I wanted to be on those roller skates.
我很想穿上那些溜冰鞋。

514
00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:57.170
I wanted to zip through.
我想滑着穿过去。

515
00:22:57.330 --> 00:22:58.410
I was so excited.
我当时太兴奋了。

516
00:22:58.410 --> 00:22:59.570
It looked so fun.
看起来太好玩了。

517
00:22:59.590 --> 00:22:59.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

518
00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:02.950
But it made sense that my character would not want to participate.
但我的角色不想参与也是合情合理的。

519
00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:04.850
But I still got to be in it.
不过我还是参与了其中。

520
00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:08.130
You know, I was glad that at least I had that little moment with Daryl
你知道，我很高兴至少我和达里尔有那一小段戏，

521
00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:11.010
and I yelled at the camera and slammed the door.
我对着镜头大喊大叫，还摔上了门。

522
00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:12.710
So we were in there the whole time.
所以我们全程都在那里。

523
00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.790
And as the camera went past us into the kitchen,
当镜头经过我们进入厨房时，

524
00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:16.970
we got a little bit of a break.
我们稍微休息了一下。

525
00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:21.110
But I have a great memory of that day because it was pretty relaxing.
但我对那天记忆犹新，因为那天相当轻松。

526
00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:25.290
I didn't actually have to do any heavy lifting in the Lip Dub.
在“对嘴演唱”里，我其实不需要做任何重活。

527
00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:26.790
I kind of got to watch it.
我算是旁观者。

528
00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:29.550
And you know Craig is such an easy person to hang out with.
而且你知道克雷格是个很好相处的人。

529
00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:30.470
We had a fun time.
我们玩得很开心。

530
00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.770
We were sort of like the goldfish in the glass bowl,
我们就像玻璃缸里的金鱼，

531
00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:35.450
like watching the humans go by.
看着人类从旁边经过。

532
00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:36.610
Jenna, what about you?
珍娜，你呢？

533
00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:37.170
Did you have fun?
你玩得开心吗？

534
00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:38.690
You got to dance and you love to dance.
你跳了舞，你很喜欢跳舞。

535
00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:39.750
You got to do a shimmy.
你还跳了扭臀舞。

536
00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:40.390
I know.
我知道。

537
00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:41.390
But you had to go backwards.
但你必须倒着走。

538
00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:42.130
Was that hard?
那很难吗？

539
00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:43.450
That was really tricky.
那确实非常棘手。

540
00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:47.670
So it was a little stressful because Ed and I had to start it off.
所以压力有点大，因为我和艾德必须负责开场。

541
00:23:47.770 --> 00:23:50.850
And if we didn't start off with the right timing, then forget it.
如果我们开场的时机不对，那就完了。

542
00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:52.690
We should just not even continue.
我们干脆就不用继续了。

543
00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:55.390
And that's really me pulling the blinds.
那确实是我在拉百叶窗。

544
00:23:55.490 --> 00:24:00.450
And then I had to dance backwards into a very specific spot
然后我必须倒着跳到一个非常具体的位置，

545
00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:03.470
where I'm hiding people behind me who can jump out.
在那里我身后藏着人，他们可以跳出来。

546
00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:08.310
So that was like a big choreography between me and Matt Soane,
所以那是我和我们的摄像师马特·索恩之间的一场大型编舞。

547
00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:09.270
our camera operator.
我们的摄像师。

548
00:24:09.270 --> 00:24:15.070
And you can see me glance out of the corner of my eye because I was worried I was going
你可以看到我用眼角余光瞥了一眼，因为我担心

549
00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:18.390
to run into the little chair at reception when I'm going back.
倒退的时候会撞到接待处的小椅子上。

550
00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.510
If you look closely, I had to look.
如果你仔细看，我确实必须看一眼。

551
00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:22.610
I was really afraid I was going to run into it.
我当时真的很怕我会撞上去。

552
00:24:22.610 --> 00:24:26.190
But I think all of those moments were because exactly of what Danny said.
但我认为所有那些时刻正是因为丹尼所说的那样。

553
00:24:26.570 --> 00:24:29.210
This is like paper company.
这就像造纸公司一样。

554
00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:31.690
I bet Danny would have loved it if I ran into the chair.
我敢打赌，如果我撞到那把椅子，丹尼一定会很开心。

555
00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:33.010
He would have been like, that's fine.
他会觉得，那没关系。

556
00:24:33.130 --> 00:24:33.310
Yeah.
是啊。

557
00:24:33.310 --> 00:24:36.550
But yes, like you said, it was really, really choreographed.
但没错，就像你说的，那确实经过了非常精心的编排。

558
00:24:36.630 --> 00:24:41.650
Except at the end, that stuff of us, we're just improvising and dancing and throwing streamers
除了结尾，我们即兴发挥、跳舞、抛洒彩带的那部分，

559
00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:42.090
and stuff.
还有其他东西。

560
00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:45.010
And so that was a relief once we got to that point.
所以一旦到了那个阶段，我们就如释重负了。

561
00:24:45.610 --> 00:24:51.670
We also, speaking of that ending part, had a fan catch from Cecily G in New Mexico.
说到结尾那部分，我们还有一位来自新墨西哥州的粉丝塞西莉·G捕捉到了一个细节。

562
00:24:52.090 --> 00:24:57.810
At two minutes and 19 seconds, I have a cheesy John Krasinski jumping up and down catch.
在两分十九秒的时候，我有一个约翰·卡拉辛斯基那种俗气的蹦蹦跳跳的镜头。

563
00:24:59.010 --> 00:25:01.930
She said he's doing his bust out some of his dance moves.
她说他在展示他的一些舞步。

564
00:25:02.110 --> 00:25:02.250
Yeah.
是啊。

565
00:25:02.610 --> 00:25:05.030
The same kind of stuff he did in Cafe Disco.
和他当年在《迪斯科咖啡馆》里跳的一样。

566
00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:07.510
I looked for it and it's great.
我找来看了，真的很棒。

567
00:25:07.750 --> 00:25:09.110
I'll have to go look for it.
我也得去看看。

568
00:25:09.610 --> 00:25:12.910
I was really curious about Creed playing the guitar.
我对克里德弹吉他那段非常好奇。

569
00:25:13.290 --> 00:25:13.610
Yeah.
是啊。

570
00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:17.210
Because, you know, Creed comes over to my house and plays the guitar all the time.
因为你知道，克里德经常来我家弹吉他。

571
00:25:17.410 --> 00:25:17.570
Yeah.
是啊。

572
00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:18.490
The man's amazing.
那个人太厉害了。

573
00:25:18.810 --> 00:25:23.010
So I reached out to him and I said, Creed, are you really playing that part of the song?
所以我联系了他，我说，克里德，你真的是在弹那段旋律吗？

574
00:25:23.130 --> 00:25:24.230
Are you really playing the guitar?
你真的在弹吉他吗？

575
00:25:28.490 --> 00:25:33.410
I'm approximating what the notes would look like and it looks real because I can actually
他说我是在模拟音符看起来的样子，看起来很真实，因为我确实会弹吉他，

576
00:25:33.410 --> 00:25:37.490
play the guitar, but I'm not synced up to where the music would be.
但我弹的节奏和音乐并没有同步。

577
00:25:37.750 --> 00:25:38.570
Oh, interesting.
哦，真有意思。

578
00:25:38.950 --> 00:25:39.110
Yeah.
是啊。

579
00:25:39.690 --> 00:25:39.910
Oh.
哦。

580
00:25:39.910 --> 00:25:44.710
So, fakie playing by a real person who can play on a real guitar.
所以，是一个真正会弹吉他的人在假装弹奏。

581
00:25:44.970 --> 00:25:48.170
It really looked to me like he was playing the notes.
在我看来，他弹得真的很像那么回事。

582
00:25:48.370 --> 00:25:48.650
Exactly.
确实。

583
00:25:48.970 --> 00:25:49.190
Yeah.
是啊。

584
00:25:49.370 --> 00:25:49.950
I'm impressed.
我印象深刻。

585
00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:52.890
Well, our final question is this.
好了，我们的最后一个问题是这个。

586
00:25:52.890 --> 00:25:58.130
Was Toby really behind the camera or was his voice added in post?
托比当时真的在摄像机后面吗？还是他的声音是后期配上去的？

587
00:25:58.990 --> 00:26:00.790
His voice was added in poSt.
他的声音是后期配上去的。

588
00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:05.390
The camera was operated by our cinematographer, Matt Soan.
摄像机是由我们的摄影指导马特·索恩操作的。

589
00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:08.610
I don't even think Paul was standing behind the camera that day.
我甚至不觉得那天保罗站在摄像机后面。

590
00:26:09.390 --> 00:26:11.130
I don't have a memory of it, Paul.
我不记得了，保罗。

591
00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:11.650
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

592
00:26:11.770 --> 00:26:12.250
Were you there?
你在场吗？

593
00:26:12.530 --> 00:26:13.630
You're so quiet.
你太安静了。

594
00:26:14.310 --> 00:26:19.110
I do love, though, that they made it Toby's voice because by doing that, then the whole entire
不过我真的很喜欢他们用了托比的声音，因为这样一来，整个办公室的人都参与进来了。

595
00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:20.270
office participated.
没错。

596
00:26:20.530 --> 00:26:20.850
Yes.
是的。

597
00:26:21.190 --> 00:26:21.510
Yes.
是的。

598
00:26:22.250 --> 00:26:27.130
Kelly Cantley shared that she walked around the room with Matt while they were filming,
凯莉·坎特利分享说，他们在拍摄时，她和马特一起在房间里走动，

599
00:26:27.430 --> 00:26:30.850
also our boom operator, Brian Whittle, and I totally remember that.
还有我们的吊杆麦克风操作员布莱恩·惠特尔，我完全记得那一幕。

600
00:26:30.930 --> 00:26:31.690
I remember that.
我记得。

601
00:26:31.850 --> 00:26:37.070
Kelly was like, it's like she had the outline of the whole thing, and she had a stopwatch.
凯莉当时就像是掌握了整件事的流程大纲，手里还拿着秒表。

602
00:26:37.210 --> 00:26:38.410
Like, she was like, let's go.
她就像是在说，我们开始吧。

603
00:26:38.670 --> 00:26:38.930
Yeah.
没错。

604
00:26:39.130 --> 00:26:43.050
They were like this little trio clump just kind of moving through.
他们就像一个小三人组，聚在一起穿行其中。

605
00:26:43.430 --> 00:26:44.530
Keeping us on track.
确保我们按计划进行。

606
00:26:44.890 --> 00:26:50.350
But we also had our second AD, Stephanie, hiding behind the reception desk.
但我们还有第二助理导演斯蒂芬妮，躲在接待台后面。

607
00:26:50.350 --> 00:26:51.530
She was giving cues.
她在负责给提示。

608
00:26:52.030 --> 00:26:56.570
Our PA Chuck was hiding behind that door over by accounting that nobody goes in.
我们的制片助理查克躲在会计室旁边那扇没人进去的门后。

609
00:26:56.690 --> 00:27:01.290
And I remember he would peek out and give the cue when the guys were coming back in through
我记得他会探出头来，在大家从厨房回来时给个提示，

610
00:27:01.290 --> 00:27:02.890
the kitchen so we could be ready.
这样我们就能做好准备。

611
00:27:03.090 --> 00:27:03.250
Right.
对。

612
00:27:03.250 --> 00:27:06.450
It was just, it was this whole machine.
这简直就像一台精密的机器。

613
00:27:06.690 --> 00:27:10.730
And some of the dancers were hidden to kind of remind us what we were supposed to do.
还有一些舞者躲在暗处，提醒我们该做什么。

614
00:27:10.850 --> 00:27:11.870
The magician was hidden.
魔术师也躲了起来。

615
00:27:12.290 --> 00:27:18.870
Gosh, I wish we had like actual documentary footage of all the people it took to pull this off.
天哪，真希望我们有纪录片素材，记录下为了完成这一切所动用的人力。

616
00:27:18.950 --> 00:27:19.170
Yeah.
是啊。

617
00:27:19.390 --> 00:27:21.610
You guys, thanks so much for sending in your questions.
各位，非常感谢你们发来的问题。

618
00:27:21.610 --> 00:27:23.450
That was really fun to break down.
拆解这一集真的很有趣。

619
00:27:23.610 --> 00:27:24.830
It was so much fun to do.
