00:40:29.490 --> 00:40:36.630
I asked Randy about it, and he said that, at first, this was flagged by standards and practices.
我问过兰迪，他说起初这被审查部门标记了。

935
00:40:36.790 --> 00:40:42.990
Because if you want to use a real product, you have to clear it with the NBC ad sales department.
因为如果你想使用真实产品，必须先通过NBC广告销售部门的审核。

936
00:40:43.290 --> 00:40:50.850
Because if they had an advertiser who might be a competitor, you know,
因为如果他们有竞争对手的广告商，你知道的，

937
00:40:50.850 --> 00:40:58.550
then that person who had bought ad time would definitely not want to see free advertising on a show.
那么买了广告时段的人肯定不想在节目里看到免费的广告。

938
00:40:58.690 --> 00:40:58.850
Right.
没错。

939
00:40:59.010 --> 00:41:00.790
Like if you're the guys at Pete's Coffee.
就像如果你是皮特咖啡的人。

940
00:41:01.330 --> 00:41:01.730
Yeah.
是啊。

941
00:41:01.770 --> 00:41:03.430
Or Coffee Bean.
或者咖啡豆品牌。

942
00:41:03.630 --> 00:41:04.750
You're like, hey, hold on a second.
你会说，嘿，等一下。

943
00:41:05.050 --> 00:41:06.230
Get that Starbucks out of there.
把那个星巴克拿走。

944
00:41:06.470 --> 00:41:11.490
Well, I guess coffee chains were not actually huge ad buyers at the time.
好吧，我想当时咖啡连锁店并不是主要的广告买家。

945
00:41:11.970 --> 00:41:12.450
Really?
真的吗？

946
00:41:12.630 --> 00:41:12.950
Yes.
是的。

947
00:41:13.150 --> 00:41:13.390
Wow.
哇。

948
00:41:13.450 --> 00:41:14.270
That's what Randy said.
兰迪是这么说的。

949
00:41:14.290 --> 00:41:15.190
That's how old we are.
这就是我们有多老了。

950
00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:16.550
That's how old the show is.
这就是这部剧有多老了。

951
00:41:16.650 --> 00:41:16.930
Yes.
是的。

952
00:41:17.130 --> 00:41:18.330
We had flip phones.
我们那时候用的是翻盖手机。

953
00:41:18.570 --> 00:41:19.950
There was no Instagram.
当时还没有 Instagram。

954
00:41:19.950 --> 00:41:23.370
Instagram and coffee companies weren't that big of a deal.
Instagram 和咖啡公司那时候还没那么大影响力。

955
00:41:23.670 --> 00:41:23.850
Yeah.
没错。

956
00:41:24.170 --> 00:41:26.570
And so I guess there were no conflicts.
所以我猜当时没什么冲突。

957
00:41:27.150 --> 00:41:30.850
And we were able to get approval to use real Starbucks cups.
我们当时获准使用了真正的星巴克杯子。

958
00:41:31.130 --> 00:41:31.430
Wow.
哇。

959
00:41:31.770 --> 00:41:32.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

960
00:41:32.390 --> 00:41:37.510
You know about the whole Starbucks cup on the set of Game of Thrones that made it into the Game of Thrones episode.
你知道《权力的游戏》片场那个星巴克杯子穿帮进剧集里的事吧。

961
00:41:37.610 --> 00:41:38.030
I do.
我知道。

962
00:41:38.350 --> 00:41:38.710
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

963
00:41:38.990 --> 00:41:43.310
I can't believe they haven't gone back and, like, wiped that out.
真不敢相信他们居然没回去把那个镜头修掉。

964
00:41:44.310 --> 00:41:49.550
It's not, like, such a lore of the show that it's like an Easter egg that you're just going to keep it in forever.
那又不是什么剧集背景设定，也不是那种非要留着当彩蛋的东西。

965
00:41:49.550 --> 00:41:51.270
Your winter is coming, and so is your Starbucks.
凛冬将至，星巴克也随之而至。

966
00:41:53.350 --> 00:41:59.930
There's now a series of talking heads that are really funny, but basically the theme is everyone hates Luke and that Luke sucks.
现在有一系列采访片段非常搞笑，主题基本就是大家都讨厌卢克，觉得卢克烂透了。

967
00:42:00.610 --> 00:42:00.830
Yeah.
是啊。

968
00:42:00.830 --> 00:42:06.110
In the kitchen, Andy is going to confront Michael and just say, Luke is the worSt.
在厨房里，安迪打算去和迈克尔对质，直接说卢克是最差劲的。

969
00:42:06.290 --> 00:42:08.130
He needs to be fired, Michael.
他必须被开除，迈克尔。

970
00:42:08.570 --> 00:42:10.910
But Michael's just kind of hedging.
但迈克尔一直在打马虎眼。

971
00:42:11.130 --> 00:42:11.230
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

972
00:42:11.230 --> 00:42:12.410
He's like, he's not that bad.
他觉得，他没那么糟。

973
00:42:12.690 --> 00:42:14.370
That other intern we had was worse.
我们之前那个实习生更差劲。

974
00:42:14.950 --> 00:42:16.710
Lady, I need to talk about this.
女士，我得谈谈这件事。

975
00:42:16.890 --> 00:42:17.910
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

976
00:42:18.350 --> 00:42:20.010
Steve's holding an apple in his scene.
史蒂夫在这一幕里手里拿着个苹果。

977
00:42:20.150 --> 00:42:22.810
He's got a coffee in one hand and an apple in the other.
他一只手拿着咖啡，另一只手拿着个苹果。

978
00:42:23.310 --> 00:42:24.590
I went to the script.
我查了剧本。

979
00:42:24.810 --> 00:42:27.210
I'm like, did this apple have a story?
我在想，这个苹果有什么故事吗？

980
00:42:27.910 --> 00:42:31.870
No, it's just, I guess he went to the kitchen to get an apple.
没有，我猜他只是去厨房拿了个苹果。

981
00:42:32.050 --> 00:42:33.070
I thought it was interesting.
我觉得这很有意思。

982
00:42:33.410 --> 00:42:34.410
This is, like, interesting.
这挺有趣的。

983
00:42:34.650 --> 00:42:36.010
Why is Michael holding an apple?
迈克尔为什么要拿个苹果？

984
00:42:36.150 --> 00:42:36.790
Interesting choice.
有趣的抉择。

985
00:42:37.170 --> 00:42:38.690
Well, I mean, I don't know.
嗯，我是说，我不知道。

986
00:42:38.890 --> 00:42:39.810
Apple and coffee.
苹果配咖啡。

987
00:42:40.250 --> 00:42:40.730
Hmm.
嗯。

988
00:42:40.910 --> 00:42:42.110
Sounds gross to me.
听起来真恶心。

989
00:42:42.550 --> 00:42:48.430
We are now going to start a whole storyline that is really centered around Pam at the core.
我们现在要开启一条以帕姆为核心的故事线。

990
00:42:48.430 --> 00:42:51.750
However, Dwight has this impressive ring of keys.
不过，德怀特有一串令人印象深刻的钥匙。

991
00:42:51.930 --> 00:42:52.850
I mean, it's ridiculous.
我是说，那太荒谬了。

992
00:42:52.850 --> 00:42:53.850
It's huge.
太大了。

993
00:42:54.050 --> 00:42:55.290
He has all these keys.
他有那么多钥匙。

994
00:42:55.590 --> 00:42:59.710
And Jim is doing basically classic Jim prankage.
而吉姆基本上是在搞经典的吉姆式恶作剧。

995
00:43:00.310 --> 00:43:00.570
Yes.
没错。

996
00:43:00.810 --> 00:43:02.950
Jim has a bunch of extra keys in his desk.
吉姆在办公桌里藏了一堆多余的钥匙。

997
00:43:03.110 --> 00:43:09.870
When he gets Dwight to go check for raccoons in the wall, he tries to add a few extra keys to the key ring.
当他骗德怀特去墙里检查有没有浣熊时，他试图往那串钥匙上多加几把。

998
00:43:10.050 --> 00:43:14.130
His goal is, very similar to when he was putting the nickels in Dwight's phone receiver.
他的目的，和当初往德怀特电话听筒里塞硬币时非常像。

999
00:43:14.330 --> 00:43:15.090
Oh, amazing.
哦，太棒了。

1000
00:43:15.190 --> 00:43:15.930
It's my favorite prank.
这是我最喜欢的恶作剧。

1001
00:43:15.990 --> 00:43:16.310
Me too.
我也是。

1002
00:43:16.310 --> 00:43:24.310
Personally, he's going to put so many extra keys, like one a day, two a day, onto this key ring that eventually his pants will fall down.
照他那样，他会往钥匙扣上加好多额外的钥匙，一天一把两把的，最后裤子都要被坠掉了。

1003
00:43:24.490 --> 00:43:25.130
That was his goal.
那正是他的目的。

1004
00:43:25.550 --> 00:43:28.410
Well, Jim has a talking head that said, what happened to me this summer?
吉姆有个访谈镜头说，我这个夏天经历了什么？

1005
00:43:28.650 --> 00:43:29.550
Dwight bought the building.
德怀特买下了这栋楼。

1006
00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:32.490
So, actually, this has been the busiest summer of my life.
所以实际上，这是我人生中最忙碌的一个夏天。

1007
00:43:32.630 --> 00:43:32.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1008
00:43:33.150 --> 00:43:34.170
He had to make plans.
他得制定计划。

1009
00:43:34.370 --> 00:43:35.670
Lots of prank plans.
好多恶作剧计划。

1010
00:43:36.150 --> 00:43:38.570
Pam finds it hilarious and starts laughing.
帕姆觉得这很有趣，开始大笑。

1011
00:43:38.810 --> 00:43:40.410
And Dwight busts Jim.
然后德怀特抓住了吉姆。

1012
00:43:40.690 --> 00:43:40.890
Yeah.
没错。

1013
00:43:41.590 --> 00:43:44.790
We had a fan question from Sarah C in Lubbock, Texas.
我们收到一个来自德克萨斯州拉伯克市萨拉·C的粉丝提问。

1014
00:43:45.570 --> 00:43:49.870
Does Rain throw real keys at John's head, or are they fakie keys?
雷恩扔向约翰头部的钥匙是真的，还是道具钥匙？

1015
00:43:50.190 --> 00:43:51.530
One of them hit him.
其中一把砸中了他。

1016
00:43:51.810 --> 00:43:53.510
And you hear like a thump.
你都能听到那种闷响。

1017
00:43:53.850 --> 00:43:54.190
I know.
我知道。

1018
00:43:54.190 --> 00:43:55.690
I was wondering the same thing.
我也在想同样的问题。

1019
00:43:56.150 --> 00:43:58.410
I swear they were real keys.
我发誓那是真钥匙。

1020
00:43:58.490 --> 00:43:58.830
Same.
我也是。

1021
00:43:59.290 --> 00:44:00.930
Because I have this memory.
因为我有这段记忆。

1022
00:44:01.210 --> 00:44:03.170
Rain was kind of throwing them at John's cheSt.
雷恩当时是往约翰的胸口扔的。

1023
00:44:03.390 --> 00:44:03.570
Yeah.
对。

1024
00:44:03.750 --> 00:44:04.350
In the scene.
在那场戏里。

1025
00:44:04.350 --> 00:44:07.390
But then, I swear it was this take.
但后来，我发誓就是在那一条拍摄中。

1026
00:44:07.630 --> 00:44:10.970
One of them just accidentally kind of like flew at John's head.
其中一把不小心飞向了约翰的头部。

1027
00:44:11.830 --> 00:44:13.390
And they stopped.
然后他们停了下来。

1028
00:44:13.710 --> 00:44:15.350
And John was like, dude.
约翰说，老兄。

1029
00:44:15.550 --> 00:44:17.670
And Rain was like, I'm so sorry.
雷恩说，我太抱歉了。

1030
00:44:17.830 --> 00:44:18.710
He's like, it's okay.
他说，没关系。

1031
00:44:18.710 --> 00:44:20.010
But like, those are real.
但那些确实是真的。

1032
00:44:20.910 --> 00:44:21.870
And yes.
没错。

1033
00:44:22.110 --> 00:44:25.650
So, I totally have that memory of shooting that scene.
所以，我完全记得拍摄那场戏的情景。

1034
00:44:26.450 --> 00:44:28.090
But I think they're real, too.
但我认为它们也是真的。

1035
00:44:28.290 --> 00:44:29.510
I have the same memory.
我有同样的记忆。

1036
00:44:30.330 --> 00:44:33.330
And also, if you watch John's reaction.
而且，如果你观察约翰的反应。

1037
00:44:33.750 --> 00:44:34.750
That's what I mean.
我指的就是那个。

1038
00:44:34.990 --> 00:44:35.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1039
00:44:35.670 --> 00:44:38.510
Well, you know, this is interesting because Pam feels really bad.
嗯，你知道，这很有趣，因为帕姆感到非常内疚。

1040
00:44:38.670 --> 00:44:41.370
And Jim is bummed out that his prank didn't go.
而吉姆因为恶作剧没成功而感到沮丧。

1041
00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:49.030
And BJ talked on the commentary about how they had to get creative with conflict scenes for Jim and Pam now that they're a happily married couple.
BJ在评论音轨里谈到，既然吉姆和帕姆现在是一对幸福的已婚夫妇，他们必须在冲突戏份上发挥创意。

1042
00:44:49.230 --> 00:44:50.450
I thought it was really interesting.
我觉得这非常有趣。

1043
00:44:50.450 --> 00:44:51.190
Let's listen.
我们来听听看。

1044
00:44:52.190 --> 00:44:57.250
So, this was something we thought of because we like when Jim and Pam have stories.
所以，这是我们想到的点子，因为我们喜欢吉姆和帕姆有故事可讲。

1045
00:44:57.410 --> 00:44:59.010
But we don't want to invent fights.
但我们不想凭空捏造争吵。

1046
00:44:59.150 --> 00:45:00.890
They're a couple that gets along really well.
他们是一对相处得非常融洽的夫妻。

1047
00:45:01.250 --> 00:45:02.810
And we like stories between them.
我们喜欢他们之间的故事。

1048
00:45:02.910 --> 00:45:05.730
But we don't always want them having conflict because that's not real.
但我们不想总是让他们产生冲突，因为那不真实。

1049
00:45:05.890 --> 00:45:07.490
So, what would be a light conflict?
所以，什么样的冲突才算轻微的呢？

1050
00:45:07.830 --> 00:45:08.230
Right.
没错。

1051
00:45:08.230 --> 00:45:09.930
It's real but not sad.
这很真实，但并不悲伤。

1052
00:45:10.410 --> 00:45:10.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1053
00:45:11.350 --> 00:45:12.270
Isn't that interesting?
这难道不有趣吗？

1054
00:45:12.570 --> 00:45:15.190
That they had to find ways for Jim and Pam to have storylines.
他们得想办法给吉姆和帕姆安排剧情线。

1055
00:45:15.190 --> 00:45:23.010
And this sort of Pam trying to do right by Jim with this prank was one of those light conflict storylines.
而帕姆试图通过这个恶作剧来善待吉姆，就是那种轻松的冲突剧情之一。

1056
00:45:23.590 --> 00:45:26.490
Well, we also had a fan catch from Ashley W.
嗯，我们还收到了一位粉丝阿什莉·W的发现。

1057
00:45:26.510 --> 00:45:28.830
in Oklahoma for the scene.
来自俄克拉荷马州，关于那个场景的。

1058
00:45:29.050 --> 00:45:30.370
You're going to like it, Angela.
你会喜欢的，安吉拉。

1059
00:45:30.670 --> 00:45:31.090
Okay.
好的。

1060
00:45:31.510 --> 00:45:32.630
Here's what Ashley said.
阿什莉是这么说的。

1061
00:45:33.030 --> 00:45:35.350
Pam's desk plant has a bow on it.
帕姆办公桌上的植物上系着一个蝴蝶结。

1062
00:45:35.670 --> 00:45:37.150
It's like a gift bow.
就像礼品包装上的那种。

1063
00:45:37.530 --> 00:45:39.930
Are these plants gifts from someone?
这些植物是某人送的礼物吗？

1064
00:45:40.290 --> 00:45:42.690
Does she have a plant subscription box?
她订购了植物订阅盒吗？

1065
00:45:42.690 --> 00:45:45.930
Maybe that's why they were constantly changing.
也许这就是它们一直在变的原因。

1066
00:45:46.610 --> 00:45:47.010
Wait.
等等。

1067
00:45:47.390 --> 00:45:50.090
Is there such a thing as a plant subscription box?
真的有植物订阅盒这种东西吗？

1068
00:45:50.310 --> 00:45:51.490
I've never heard of that.
我从没听说过。

1069
00:45:51.990 --> 00:45:54.450
Could I get plants sent to me every month?
我能每个月都收到寄来的植物吗？

1070
00:45:54.670 --> 00:45:55.930
You've never heard of this?
你从没听说过这个？

1071
00:45:56.190 --> 00:45:56.630
No.
没有。

1072
00:45:57.430 --> 00:45:59.690
It's like, you know, like cheese of the month.
就像，你知道的，像每月精选奶酪那样。

1073
00:45:59.870 --> 00:46:01.270
You can get flowers of the month.
你可以订购每月鲜花。

1074
00:46:01.470 --> 00:46:02.290
Plant of the month.
每月植物。

1075
00:46:02.530 --> 00:46:03.250
Wine of the month.
每月红酒。

1076
00:46:03.390 --> 00:46:03.630
Okay.
好吧。

1077
00:46:04.050 --> 00:46:04.950
Cheese, wine.
奶酪，红酒。

1078
00:46:05.270 --> 00:46:06.570
I guess flowers make sense.
我觉得鲜花还说得过去。

1079
00:46:06.690 --> 00:46:09.830
But I didn't know you could get a whole living plant like in a pot.
但我不知道你还能收到一整盆活生生的植物。

1080
00:46:10.090 --> 00:46:11.230
I mean, I believe it.
我是说，我相信有。

1081
00:46:12.370 --> 00:46:14.010
Um, I want one.
嗯，我想要一个。

1082
00:46:14.310 --> 00:46:14.790
Okay.
好的。

1083
00:46:15.030 --> 00:46:16.450
Plant subscription box.
植物订阅盒。

1084
00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:18.130
Coming your way, lady.
这就给你安排上，女士。

1085
00:46:18.830 --> 00:46:22.250
Josh is going to be like, Ange, plants are all over the house.
乔什肯定会说，安吉，家里到处都是植物了。

1086
00:46:23.710 --> 00:46:25.430
I had a flowers of the month.
我曾经订过每月鲜花。

1087
00:46:25.690 --> 00:46:27.370
Lee got it for me for Christmas one year.
有一年圣诞节李送给我的。

1088
00:46:27.530 --> 00:46:29.430
And every month I got fresh flowers.
每个月我都能收到新鲜的花。

1089
00:46:29.610 --> 00:46:31.430
It was so amazing.
那真是太棒了。

1090
00:46:32.190 --> 00:46:32.630
I know.
我知道。

1091
00:46:32.970 --> 00:46:34.570
Well, I'll tell you what, Ashley.
好吧，阿什莉，我告诉你。

1092
00:46:34.790 --> 00:46:37.570
I don't know if there was a subscription box,
我不知道当时有没有订阅盒，

1093
00:46:37.610 --> 00:46:39.870
but I'll tell you my backstory for that plant.
但我可以告诉你那盆植物的背景故事。

1094
00:46:40.490 --> 00:46:46.350
Do you remember when Jim let Pam's plant die on her desk when she went on maternity leave?
你还记得帕姆休产假时，吉姆让她的植物枯死了吗？

1095
00:46:46.510 --> 00:46:49.070
So you think Jim bought Pam a new plant?
所以你觉得是吉姆给帕姆买了一盆新植物？

1096
00:46:49.170 --> 00:46:49.590
I do.
我是这么认为的。

1097
00:46:49.810 --> 00:46:50.570
Oh, I like that.
哦，我喜欢这个解释。

1098
00:46:50.590 --> 00:46:52.230
And that's why there was a little bow on it.
这就是为什么上面有个小蝴蝶结。

1099
00:46:52.330 --> 00:46:56.990
And I think she didn't take the bow off because it reminded her of Jim's thoughtfulness.
而且我觉得她没把蝴蝶结摘掉，是因为它提醒了她吉姆的体贴。

1100
00:46:57.590 --> 00:46:58.490
I like that.
我喜欢这个说法。

1101
00:46:59.350 --> 00:47:03.090
Well, there is someone in the office who you don't want to tick off, and that is Phyllis.
办公室里有一个人你绝对不想惹，那就是菲利斯。

1102
00:47:03.390 --> 00:47:04.390
Oh, that's right.
哦，没错。

1103
00:47:04.390 --> 00:47:06.190
And Luke has crossed Phyllis.
而卢克惹到了菲利斯。

1104
00:47:06.370 --> 00:47:12.410
She lost an account because she's pretty sure Luke did not send the samples he was supposed to.
她丢了一个客户，因为她很确定卢克根本没寄出他本该寄出的样品。

1105
00:47:12.710 --> 00:47:13.330
That's right.
没错。

1106
00:47:13.670 --> 00:47:16.770
Lehigh Motors has not gotten their samples.
利哈伊汽车公司还没收到他们的样品。

1107
00:47:17.470 --> 00:47:22.670
He blows off Phyllis, and then, you know, he's just like playing video games on Meredith's computer.
他敷衍菲利斯，然后呢，你知道，他就只会在梅雷迪思的电脑上玩电子游戏。

1108
00:47:23.170 --> 00:47:24.990
Everyone's getting so frustrated with Luke.
大家对卢克都感到非常沮丧。

1109
00:47:25.170 --> 00:47:26.750
Michael sends him to get ice cream.
迈克尔打发他去买冰淇淋了。

1110
00:47:27.450 --> 00:47:31.990
At 8 minutes and 49 seconds, Angela, you are not at your desk in the background of this scene.
在8分49秒的时候，安吉拉，这一幕的背景里你不在工位上。

1111
00:47:32.550 --> 00:47:33.350
I noticed.
我注意到了。

1112
00:47:33.690 --> 00:47:35.130
I bet I had gone to the bathroom.
我敢打赌我当时是去洗手间了。

1113
00:47:35.290 --> 00:47:36.630
Where have you sneaked away to, lady?
你溜到哪儿去了，女士？

1114
00:47:36.630 --> 00:47:39.590
I probably talked our AD into letting me go to the bathroom.
我大概是说服了我们的助理导演让我去洗手间。

1115
00:47:39.710 --> 00:47:40.770
Like, they're not going to see me.
就觉得，他们肯定看不见我。

1116
00:47:40.930 --> 00:47:41.390
I know.
我知道。

1117
00:47:42.270 --> 00:47:42.910
All right.
好吧。

1118
00:47:43.110 --> 00:47:47.830
We are 10 minutes into this episode, and we are going to move to a scene in the conference room,
这一集已经播到10分钟了，我们要转到会议室的场景了，

1119
00:47:47.830 --> 00:47:50.450
I noticed, with the conference table.
我注意到了，有会议桌的那种。

1120
00:47:50.670 --> 00:47:51.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1121
00:47:51.270 --> 00:47:53.230
Not the usual row of chairs.
不是平时那种排排坐的椅子。

1122
00:47:53.990 --> 00:47:55.230
Table is back.
桌子又回来了。

1123
00:47:56.170 --> 00:48:00.570
People are going to figure out pretty quickly that Michael is related to Luke.
大家很快就会发现迈克尔和卢克有亲戚关系。

1124
00:48:00.770 --> 00:48:02.830
Oscar accuses Michael of nepotism.
奥斯卡指责迈克尔任人唯亲。

1125
00:48:03.230 --> 00:48:07.610
This whole conference room scene is delicious and amazing.
整个会议室的戏份真是太精彩、太棒了。

1126
00:48:08.130 --> 00:48:11.870
During this rewatch, lady, I love our conference room scenes.
在这次重温过程中，女士，我超爱我们的会议室戏份。

1127
00:48:12.070 --> 00:48:12.370
Same.
我也是。

1128
00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:14.790
I loved doing our conference room scenes.
我喜欢拍我们的会议室戏份。

1129
00:48:15.030 --> 00:48:19.090
I used to feel bad for Steve because I knew how much work they were for him.
我以前常为史蒂夫感到难过，因为我知道这些戏对他来说工作量有多大。

1130
00:48:19.230 --> 00:48:21.690
We'd be in there all day, and he would be the leader.
我们得在那儿待上一整天，而他必须是主导者。

1131
00:48:21.970 --> 00:48:23.470
He would be driving the scene.
他得掌控整场戏。

1132
00:48:23.470 --> 00:48:27.970
He would have the majority of the dialogue, and all we had to do was chime in with a line
他要承担大部分台词，而我们只需要偶尔插上一两句，

1133
00:48:27.970 --> 00:48:28.510
or two here.
或者在这里说上一两句。

1134
00:48:28.730 --> 00:48:32.090
And basically, everyone that worked at Dunder Mifflin was always versus Michael.
基本上，邓德·米夫林的所有员工总是站在迈克尔的对立面。

1135
00:48:32.450 --> 00:48:32.690
Yes.
没错。

1136
00:48:32.870 --> 00:48:34.390
But they are delightful.
但这些戏真的很令人愉悦。

1137
00:48:34.690 --> 00:48:37.150
I get so excited every time we go to the conference room.
每次我们要去会议室拍戏，我都特别兴奋。

1138
00:48:37.610 --> 00:48:43.170
At 10 minutes and 19 seconds in this conference room scene, Rain is drinking water from his pouch.
在会议室这场戏的10分19秒，雷恩正在用他的水袋喝水。

1139
00:48:44.150 --> 00:48:50.290
I swear to God, I remember that he drank real water from that pouch all day long.
我发誓，我记得他那天一整天都在那个水袋里喝真水。

1140
00:48:50.430 --> 00:48:52.290
I remember he had to pee all day long.
我记得他那天一整天都在上厕所。

1141
00:48:52.570 --> 00:48:53.530
No, it's true.
不，这是真的。

1142
00:48:54.010 --> 00:48:55.350
He was not fakie drinking.
他不是假装在喝水。

1143
00:48:55.590 --> 00:48:56.310
He was not fakie drinking.
他不是假装在喝水。

1144
00:48:56.550 --> 00:48:58.830
Rain is very method, you know, as an actor.
雷恩作为演员，你知道，非常讲究方法派表演。

1145
00:48:59.130 --> 00:49:02.810
So if he was like, if Dwight's supposed to be drinking water, I'm going to be drinking lots of water.
所以如果他觉得，如果德怀特应该在喝水，那我就要真的喝很多水。

1146
00:49:03.190 --> 00:49:03.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:49:03.990 --> 00:49:06.810
Creed has a talking head that I absolutely love.
克里德有一个我超级喜欢的个人访谈。

1148
00:49:06.810 --> 00:49:12.050
Creed says, I couldn't care less about nepotism, but I'm loving the debate.
克里德说，我才不在乎什么任人唯亲，但我很喜欢看这场辩论。

1149
00:49:12.310 --> 00:49:15.690
Great minds battling it out, and I've got a front row seat.
伟大的头脑在交锋，而我正坐在前排看好戏。

1150
00:49:16.770 --> 00:49:17.570
So good.
太棒了。

1151
00:49:17.710 --> 00:49:18.550
So good.
太棒了。

1152
00:49:19.430 --> 00:49:20.690
I mean, I'm Creed.
我是说，我是克里德。

1153
00:49:21.230 --> 00:49:21.710
Really?
真的吗？

1154
00:49:21.970 --> 00:49:24.110
You're like, I'm loving it as well.
你就像是在说，我也很喜欢它。

1155
00:49:24.530 --> 00:49:26.390
Well, lady, maybe we should take a break.
好吧，女士，也许我们该休息一下了。

1156
00:49:26.590 --> 00:49:27.010
Yeah.
没错。

1157
00:49:27.010 --> 00:49:33.050
And when we come back, Luke is going to have soy ice cream and bagel chips for everybody.
等我们回来，卢克会给大家准备豆奶冰淇淋和贝果脆片。

1158
00:49:33.390 --> 00:49:39.570
And there was a mini Michael Pam tangent that was cut from this conference room scene that I'm excited to share.
还有一段关于迈克尔和帕姆的小插曲，从会议室这场戏里剪掉了，我很期待和大家分享。

1159
00:49:39.790 --> 00:49:40.090
Ooh.
噢。

1160
00:49:51.310 --> 00:49:52.910
Well, we are back from break.
好了，我们休息回来了。

1161
00:49:53.150 --> 00:49:55.850
Michael is continuing to defend Luke.
迈克尔还在继续维护卢克。

1162
00:49:56.010 --> 00:49:58.330
He's even comparing himself and Luke to like God and Jesus.
他甚至把自己和卢克比作上帝和耶稣。

1163
00:49:58.670 --> 00:49:59.470
That's right.
没错。

1164
00:49:59.650 --> 00:50:04.390
And Jim has this line where he says, oh, so you and Luke are God and Jesus?
吉姆有句台词说，哦，所以你和卢克是上帝和耶稣？

1165
00:50:04.890 --> 00:50:06.770
And Michael says, no, not that.
迈克尔说，不，不是那个意思。

1166
00:50:06.870 --> 00:50:09.610
I'm just saying, why does God get to do something I don't?
我只是在说，为什么上帝能做我不能做的事？

1167
00:50:09.690 --> 00:50:12.390
Why does God get to do nepotism, basically?
基本上就是，为什么上帝可以搞裙带关系？

1168
00:50:12.670 --> 00:50:12.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1169
00:50:13.090 --> 00:50:16.450
And then Oscar says, this is all hypothetical.
然后奥斯卡说，这都是假设。

1170
00:50:16.450 --> 00:50:19.470
We're talking about Luke, who is actually terrible.
我们在说卢克，他其实很糟糕。

1171
00:50:20.350 --> 00:50:27.710
And I don't know if you noticed, lady, but 11 minutes, 48 seconds, when Oscar says that line to Michael, I'm sort of smiling and shrugging.
我不知道你有没有注意到，女士，在11分48秒的时候，当奥斯卡对迈克尔说那句台词时，我好像在微笑和耸肩。

1172
00:50:27.790 --> 00:50:31.850
Like, I have a sort of out-of-context body energy.
就像我有一种脱离语境的肢体语言。

1173
00:50:32.110 --> 00:50:33.230
Yeah, like reaction.
对，就像是一种反应。

1174
00:50:33.230 --> 00:50:35.410
And at first I thought, oh, my gosh, am I breaking?
起初我心想，天哪，我是不是笑场了？

1175
00:50:35.790 --> 00:50:36.030
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1176
00:50:36.150 --> 00:50:45.790
And then I remembered, no, Pam and Michael had a bit because I suddenly had that like sense memory of shooting it and we were laughing.
后来我想起来了，不，帕姆和迈克尔有个梗，我突然有了拍摄时的记忆，我们当时都在笑。

1177
00:50:45.910 --> 00:50:47.330
Like all these memories came back.
就像所有这些记忆都回来了。

1178
00:50:47.330 --> 00:50:50.910
So I checked the shooting draft and I found it.
所以我查了拍摄剧本，找到了它。

1179
00:50:51.150 --> 00:50:53.170
Here is what would have happened.
这就是原本会发生的事情。

1180
00:50:54.470 --> 00:50:58.550
So Michael was going to say, why does God get to do something I don't?
迈克尔本来要说，为什么上帝能做我不能做的事？

1181
00:51:06.450 --> 00:51:16.850
To which Michael said, Pam, let's say you're my daughter and I'm the CEO of the world's biggest toy company, Scott's Games and Fun.
迈克尔接着说，帕姆，假设你是我的女儿，我是世界上最大的玩具公司“斯科特游戏与娱乐”的首席执行官。

1182
00:51:16.850 --> 00:51:20.870
We make funny putty, magic marbles, connectibles.
我们生产搞怪油灰、神奇弹珠、连接积木。

1183
00:51:21.250 --> 00:51:23.410
And Dwight said, what are connectibles?
德怀特问，什么是连接积木？

1184
00:51:23.690 --> 00:51:27.950
And Michael said, they're my knockoff Legos, almost as good half the price.
迈克尔说，那是我的山寨乐高，质量差不多，价格只有一半。

1185
00:51:27.950 --> 00:51:34.030
And I remember that was, we would lose it on this, like, connectibles.
我记得当时我们因为这个笑得不行，就是那个“连接积木”。

1186
00:51:34.310 --> 00:51:35.570
Like, what are connectibles?
就像是，什么是连接积木？

1187
00:51:35.650 --> 00:51:35.830
Yeah.
没错。

1188
00:51:36.490 --> 00:51:43.070
So anyway, then Michael would say, okay, one day I fall in the Sliminator and die.
总之，然后迈克尔会说，好吧，有一天我掉进“史莱姆粉碎机”里死了。

1189
00:51:43.670 --> 00:51:44.910
And we would all laugh.
然后我们都会笑。

1190
00:51:45.030 --> 00:51:48.990
Like, we could not get through this runner of Michael's toy company.
我们当时根本没法演完迈克尔这个玩具公司的桥段。

1191
00:51:49.190 --> 00:51:53.530
Oh, my God, I'm remembering this because I remember also how well thought out it was.
天哪，我记起来了，因为我记得当时这个设定有多么周全。

1192
00:51:53.570 --> 00:51:53.750
Yes.
是的。

1193
00:51:53.810 --> 00:51:58.490
He's throwing it out as just an off-the-cuff example, but it is a well-thought-out toy company.
他随口举了个例子，但那却是一家构思精巧的玩具公司。

1194
00:51:58.730 --> 00:52:02.250
He says, Pam, I left you the company.
他说，帕姆，我把公司留给了你。

1195
00:52:02.250 --> 00:52:03.630
Would you turn it down?
你会拒绝吗？

1196
00:52:03.630 --> 00:52:07.070
So in this example, Pam is Michael's daughter.
所以在这个例子里，帕姆是迈克尔的女儿。

1197
00:52:07.310 --> 00:52:11.270
And Michael's created this insanely successful toy company.
迈克尔创立了一家极其成功的玩具公司。

1198
00:52:11.470 --> 00:52:15.410
But he dies in the Sliminator and has left her the company.
但他死在了“史莱姆粉碎机”里，并把公司留给了她。

1199
00:52:15.630 --> 00:52:16.790
He's Willy Wonka.
他就是威利·旺卡。

1200
00:52:16.990 --> 00:52:20.170
He wants to know, would I turn it down?
他想知道，我会拒绝吗？

1201
00:52:20.330 --> 00:52:23.110
And Pam said, if I was unqualified, yes.
帕姆说，如果我不够格，是的。

1202
00:52:23.350 --> 00:52:27.710
To which Michael says, very seriously, but you're not.
迈克尔非常严肃地回答说，但你够格。

1203
00:52:27.870 --> 00:52:30.790
You've got an amazing mind for toys.
你在玩具方面很有天赋。

1204
00:52:31.390 --> 00:52:34.470
And then the script said, Pam looks flattered.
剧本上写着，帕姆看起来受宠若惊。

1205
00:52:34.710 --> 00:52:35.490
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1206
00:52:35.490 --> 00:52:38.350
And then Oscar said, this is all hypothetical.
然后奥斯卡说，这都是假设。

1207
00:52:38.850 --> 00:52:40.190
Oh, that's why he's not.
哦，这就是他为什么不是。

1208
00:52:40.190 --> 00:52:41.170
So that look on my face.
所以我脸上才会有那种表情。

1209
00:52:41.610 --> 00:52:44.930
But also why Oscar is saying, this is all hypothetical.
但这也是奥斯卡说这都是假设的原因。

1210
00:52:45.250 --> 00:52:46.650
Yes, this toy company.
是的，这家玩具公司。

1211
00:52:46.890 --> 00:52:51.650
But it's why when I'm sitting next to him on that line, I'm like, oh, well, thank you very.
但这就是为什么当我和他并排坐着时，我会想，哦，好吧，非常感谢。

1212
00:52:51.710 --> 00:52:55.630
You can see that I'm saying non-verbally, thank you very much, Michael.
你可以看出我是在用非语言的方式表达，非常感谢你，迈克尔。

1213
00:52:55.630 --> 00:52:58.530
But like, Pam is like, oh, well, if you say so.
但帕姆就像是，哦，好吧，既然你这么说的话。

1214
00:52:58.690 --> 00:52:59.250
That's right.
没错。

1215
00:52:59.750 --> 00:53:00.630
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1216
00:53:00.630 --> 00:53:02.290
I remember all of that now.
我现在都想起来了。

1217
00:53:02.430 --> 00:53:02.750
Yes, right?
是啊，对吧？

1218
00:53:02.930 --> 00:53:05.050
It's like you opened a folder in my brain.
就像你打开了我大脑里的一个文件夹。

1219
00:53:05.830 --> 00:53:06.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1220
00:53:06.630 --> 00:53:08.670
Yes, Michael's toy company.
是的，迈克尔的玩具公司。

1221
00:53:08.950 --> 00:53:14.270
And by the way, I went to the bloopers to see if it was in there because I know it wasn't in deleted scenes.
顺便说一下，我去看过花絮，想看看里面有没有，因为我知道删减片段里没有。

1222
00:53:14.730 --> 00:53:15.750
It's not in there.
里面没有。

1223
00:53:15.910 --> 00:53:16.830
But we were cracking up.
但我们当时笑得前仰后合。

1224
00:53:16.830 --> 00:53:17.270
There's somewhere.
肯定在某处。

1225
00:53:17.650 --> 00:53:18.030
Somewhere.
某处。

1226
00:53:18.430 --> 00:53:21.170
Well, that was a delightful trip down memory lane.
好吧，那真是一次令人愉快的怀旧之旅。

1227
00:53:21.570 --> 00:53:23.990
I do want to address something, though, with Pam.
不过，我想谈谈关于帕姆的一件事。

1228
00:53:23.990 --> 00:53:29.550
Oh, she's about to have a talking head where she says she feels awful for blowing Jim's prank.
哦，她马上要有一个采访镜头，说她因为搞砸了吉姆的恶作剧而感到非常内疚。

1229
00:53:29.750 --> 00:53:33.210
Can we talk about how fancy, fancy Pam is looking?
我们能聊聊帕姆看起来有多时髦吗？

1230
00:53:33.610 --> 00:53:35.010
What is with this hair?
这发型是怎么回事？

1231
00:53:35.190 --> 00:53:36.710
I noticed black eyeliner.
我注意到了黑色眼线。

1232
00:53:37.070 --> 00:53:38.350
I mean, fancy Pam.
我是说，时髦的帕姆。

1233
00:53:38.670 --> 00:53:40.510
You are not the only one, Angela.
安吉拉，你不是一个人。

1234
00:53:40.710 --> 00:53:41.870
We got mail about it.
我们收到了关于此事的邮件。

1235
00:53:42.330 --> 00:53:44.970
We got a fan question from Kaylee E.
我们收到了来自印第安纳波利斯的凯莉·E.

1236
00:53:45.110 --> 00:53:46.950
in Indianapolis and Kristen H.
和来自阿肯色州小石城的克里斯汀·H.

1237
00:53:47.090 --> 00:53:48.110
from Little Rock, Arkansas.
的粉丝提问。

1238
00:53:48.850 --> 00:53:51.370
Pam's look takes a big shift this season.
这一季帕姆的造型有了很大的转变。

1239
00:53:51.370 --> 00:53:56.050
And straighter hair, a tucked-in shirt, more blazers than cardigans.
头发更直了，衬衫塞进裤子里，西装外套比开衫多了。

