1721
01:14:21.230 --> 01:14:29.740
Well, on the commentary, BJ and Paul talked about the moment they knew this whole Luke-Michael storyline was going to have a payoff and work.
在评论音轨里，BJ和保罗谈到了他们意识到卢克和迈克尔这条故事线会有回报并能成功的那一刻。

1722
01:14:29.920 --> 01:14:34.860
And in particular, they talked about whose idea it was for Michael to spank Luke.
特别是，他们谈到了迈克尔打卢克屁股这个主意是谁想出来的。

1723
01:14:34.860 --> 01:14:35.780
Listen to this.
听听这个。

1724
01:14:37.960 --> 01:14:42.160
It wasn't until we had this scene that we figured we could, this episode worked.
直到拍了这场戏，我们才觉得这集成了。

1725
01:14:42.680 --> 01:14:43.120
Yeah.
是的。

1726
01:14:43.340 --> 01:14:45.320
In the writing stage, in the outlining stage.
在剧本创作阶段，在大纲阶段。

1727
01:14:46.320 --> 01:14:46.760
Yeah.
是的。

1728
01:14:46.900 --> 01:14:48.480
I was sitting in editing.
我当时坐在剪辑室里。

1729
01:14:48.760 --> 01:14:50.540
You came in with a note card.
你拿着一张笔记卡进来了。

1730
01:14:51.060 --> 01:14:52.120
Written by Aaron Schur.
是亚伦·舒尔写的。

1731
01:14:52.280 --> 01:14:53.140
Written by Aaron Schur.
是亚伦·舒尔写的。

1732
01:14:53.920 --> 01:14:55.020
It just said Michael Spanx.
上面只写着“迈克尔打屁股”。

1733
01:14:55.020 --> 01:14:55.840
Michael Spanx Luke.
迈克尔打卢克的屁股。

1734
01:14:56.260 --> 01:14:56.460
Yeah.
是的。

1735
01:14:56.640 --> 01:14:57.900
And you said, we got it.
你说，我们搞定了。

1736
01:14:58.220 --> 01:14:58.320
Yeah.
是的。

1737
01:14:58.900 --> 01:14:58.980
Awesome.
太棒了。

1738
01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:01.560
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

1739
01:15:01.560 --> 01:15:04.560
I texted Aaron and I was like, Aaron, is this true?
我给亚伦发了短信，问他：亚伦，这是真的吗？

1740
01:15:04.660 --> 01:15:06.580
And he goes, yeah, I'm pretty sure that's right.
他说，是的，我确定是这样。

1741
01:15:08.400 --> 01:15:09.480
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

1742
01:15:10.240 --> 01:15:13.540
Well, now we're going to go back over to the elevator bay.
好了，现在我们回到电梯间。

1743
01:15:14.220 --> 01:15:15.580
Dwight and Pam are stuck.
德怀特和帕姆被困住了。

1744
01:15:16.480 --> 01:15:22.260
They've managed to get a technician, a real technician, who was played by Tom Melby.
他们设法找来了一名技术员，一名真正的技术员，由汤姆·梅尔比饰演。

1745
01:15:22.520 --> 01:15:22.920
Yes.
是的。

1746
01:15:23.080 --> 01:15:24.940
Tom Melby was our stage manager.
汤姆·梅尔比是我们的舞台监督。

1747
01:15:25.200 --> 01:15:27.040
He was there the whole entire run of the show.
他在剧组待了整整一季。

1748
01:15:27.040 --> 01:15:31.700
He basically knew everything about the property where we filmed and could fix anything.
他基本上了解我们拍摄地的一切，什么都能修。

1749
01:15:32.220 --> 01:15:36.360
And I love that we put him in this episode, working on the elevator.
我很高兴我们让他在这集里出镜，修理电梯。

1750
01:15:36.580 --> 01:15:40.920
They said in the commentary that Tom was so shy, and that's why he kind of kept his head tucked down.
他们在评论音轨里说汤姆非常害羞，所以他一直低着头。

1751
01:15:41.500 --> 01:15:43.420
Well, you know, this was a fakie elevator.
嗯，你知道，这其实是个假电梯。

1752
01:15:43.840 --> 01:15:45.360
This was not real.
它不是真的。

1753
01:15:45.540 --> 01:15:52.220
And so this was a huge elaborate thing that they had to build of us being stuck between floors,
所以这是一个非常庞大且复杂的装置，他们必须搭建出来，模拟我们被困在楼层之间，

1754
01:15:53.160 --> 01:15:56.000
being up high like that with that little opening.
像那样被困在高处，还要从那个小开口钻出去。

1755
01:15:56.160 --> 01:15:56.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1756
01:15:56.500 --> 01:16:01.920
But all of it, you know, even earlier, you know, we've said the elevator doors opened and closed
但所有这些，你知道，甚至更早之前，我们说过电梯门开开关关，

1757
01:16:01.920 --> 01:16:05.540
because there was a crew person, like, doing a rope on a pulley.
那是因为有个工作人员在用绳子拉滑轮。

1758
01:16:05.760 --> 01:16:05.940
Yeah.
没错。

1759
01:16:06.040 --> 01:16:10.020
So when we had that whole moment before when the elevator's breaking down,
所以当我们之前经历电梯故障的那一整段戏时，

1760
01:16:10.220 --> 01:16:14.980
that was a very elaborate set of, like, someone was shaking the elevator,
那是一套非常复杂的装置，有人在晃动电梯，

1761
01:16:15.420 --> 01:16:17.300
someone was pulling on the pulleys.
有人在拉动滑轮。

1762
01:16:17.440 --> 01:16:20.240
It was, like, very, like, old-timey.
感觉就像是那种非常老派的把戏。

1763
01:16:20.380 --> 01:16:22.140
I was going to say, it sounds like a vaudeville show.
我正想说，听起来就像杂耍表演。

1764
01:16:22.240 --> 01:16:23.880
Yes, that's kind of what it was.
没错，差不多就是那样。

1765
01:16:23.880 --> 01:16:28.420
But we actually shot this broken elevator in a completely different spot.
但我们实际上是在一个完全不同的地方拍摄这个故障电梯的。

1766
01:16:28.420 --> 01:16:30.200
It wasn't even in our little lobby.
它甚至不在我们那个小大厅里。

1767
01:16:30.340 --> 01:16:32.980
It was over on the warehouse stage on stage four.
它是在四号摄影棚的仓库区。

1768
01:16:33.220 --> 01:16:35.000
They recreated the lobby.
他们重建了大厅。

1769
01:16:35.460 --> 01:16:36.740
Michael Gallenberg designed it.
迈克尔·加伦伯格设计的。

1770
01:16:36.860 --> 01:16:38.040
Tim James built it.
蒂姆·詹姆斯搭建的。

1771
01:16:38.140 --> 01:16:41.920
And it was on a platform that was about four feet above the stage.
它被架在一个离地约四英尺的平台上。

1772
01:16:42.240 --> 01:16:47.800
I just remember it was, like, this really cool thing that they had to build.
我只记得那是一个他们必须搭建的非常酷的东西。

1773
01:16:47.800 --> 01:16:49.680
And then I had to stand up there.
然后我就得站在上面。

1774
01:16:49.820 --> 01:16:50.860
We really were high up.
我们确实离地很高。

1775
01:16:50.960 --> 01:16:51.580
Yeah, you really were.
没错，你们确实很高。

1776
01:16:51.780 --> 01:16:53.080
I have a question for you, Angela.
安吉拉，我有个问题想问你。

1777
01:16:53.240 --> 01:16:55.680
So in this scene where Pam's stuck in the elevator with Dwight,
在帕姆和德怀特被困在电梯里的这场戏中，

1778
01:16:56.660 --> 01:16:57.460
Jim comes over.
吉姆过来了。

1779
01:16:57.580 --> 01:16:58.660
She's so proud of herself.
她对自己感到非常自豪。

1780
01:16:59.160 --> 01:17:02.240
She says, they don't call me the Bart Simpson of Scranton for nothing.
她说，他们叫我斯克兰顿的巴特·辛普森可不是白叫的。

1781
01:17:03.200 --> 01:17:05.000
Jim says, here, I'll help you down.
吉姆说，来，我帮你下来。

1782
01:17:05.180 --> 01:17:06.440
And she says, nope, it's okay.
她说，不用，没关系。

1783
01:17:06.440 --> 01:17:08.000
I'm afraid of getting cut in half.
我怕被拦腰截断。

1784
01:17:08.800 --> 01:17:09.780
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1785
01:17:09.980 --> 01:17:10.240
Okay.
好。

1786
01:17:11.280 --> 01:17:14.340
If you were stuck like Pam, would you go through the little opening
如果你像帕姆一样被困住，你会选择从那个小开口钻出去，

1787
01:17:14.340 --> 01:17:16.200
or would you be afraid of being cut in half?
还是会担心被拦腰截断？

1788
01:17:18.520 --> 01:17:20.980
I mean, I don't want to be cut in half.
我是说，我不想被拦腰截断。

1789
01:17:21.480 --> 01:17:24.220
But I think in that moment, I would just want out.
但我觉得在那一刻，我只想逃出去。

1790
01:17:24.360 --> 01:17:26.020
So I think I would go for it.
所以我认为我会试一试。

1791
01:17:26.100 --> 01:17:28.500
If I could just slip right out there, I'd probably go for it.
如果我能直接溜出去，我可能会试一试。

1792
01:17:29.360 --> 01:17:32.920
I don't think I would do it because I would just think of that scene and speed.
我觉得我不会那么做，因为我会想到电影《生死时速》里的那个场景。

1793
01:17:33.220 --> 01:17:33.580
Yes.
没错。

1794
01:17:33.760 --> 01:17:36.540
When they're stuck in the elevator and they're having the people come through.
当他们被困在电梯里，看着人们从那里钻出来的时候。

1795
01:17:36.760 --> 01:17:36.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1796
01:17:37.540 --> 01:17:38.460
You can't hesitate.
你不能犹豫。

1797
01:17:38.980 --> 01:17:39.700
It keeps falling.
电梯一直在下坠。

1798
01:17:39.700 --> 01:17:40.540
Is that it?
是这样吗？

1799
01:17:40.660 --> 01:17:41.520
You can't hesitate.
你不能犹豫。

1800
01:17:41.940 --> 01:17:46.400
I mean, they had to have me say that because they wanted the visual comic gag
我是说，他们必须让我说那句话，因为他们想要那种视觉喜剧效果。

1801
01:17:46.400 --> 01:17:48.800
of like me being in this broken elevator.
就像我被困在这部坏掉的电梯里一样。

1802
01:17:49.020 --> 01:17:50.560
Why is Pam not coming out?
为什么帕姆还不出来？

1803
01:17:50.680 --> 01:17:50.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1804
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:55.060
I probably would have already crawled out if those guys would have let me.
如果那些人肯让我出来，我可能早就爬出来了。

1805
01:17:56.100 --> 01:17:57.160
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

1806
01:17:58.260 --> 01:18:02.680
Well, wrapping up this episode, Michael has earned the respect of his coworkers.
好了，总结一下这一集，迈克尔赢得了同事们的尊重。

1807
01:18:03.140 --> 01:18:07.380
Luke was a real problem and he got rid of Luke and they're happy about it.
卢克是个大麻烦，他除掉了卢克，大家对此都很高兴。

1808
01:18:07.380 --> 01:18:10.560
They have a whole scene where they're pretending to spank each other.
他们还有一段假装互相打屁股的戏。

1809
01:18:11.480 --> 01:18:17.880
However, Gabe is not happy that Michael assaulted an employee at work.
然而，盖博对迈克尔在工作中殴打员工感到不满。

1810
01:18:17.880 --> 01:18:24.260
And to deal with it, he tells Michael he's going to need to attend six counseling sessions.
为了处理这件事，他告诉迈克尔需要参加六次心理辅导。

1811
01:18:25.140 --> 01:18:27.040
And Michael's like, that's it?
迈克尔心想，就这？

1812
01:18:27.140 --> 01:18:28.240
No problem.
没问题。

1813
01:18:28.620 --> 01:18:30.660
Except your counselor will be Toby.
但你的辅导员会是托比。

1814
01:18:32.240 --> 01:18:37.160
It's literally be fired or do six counseling sessions with Toby.
要么被解雇，要么和托比进行六次心理辅导，二选一。

1815
01:18:37.380 --> 01:18:39.360
And Michael isn't sure what he wants.
迈克尔不知道自己该怎么选。

1816
01:18:39.460 --> 01:18:42.120
He really takes a long, lingering look.
他真的看了很久，眼神久久没有移开。

1817
01:18:42.380 --> 01:18:45.020
And on the commentary, they said that was Steve.
在评论音轨里，他们说那是史蒂夫自己加的戏。

1818
01:18:45.240 --> 01:18:50.780
That choice to make that look of like, hmm, well, should I just call it quits?
那个眼神的选择，就像是在想，嗯，我是不是该干脆辞职算了？

1819
01:18:51.300 --> 01:18:57.660
This is going to lead into next week's episode, which is that counseling session between Michael and Toby.
这将引出下一集的剧情，也就是迈克尔和托比之间的那场心理辅导。

1820
01:18:57.900 --> 01:18:58.660
It is delicious.
那场戏太精彩了。

1821
01:19:00.240 --> 01:19:03.960
Before we go, Angela, we got this letter from Catherine P.
在结束之前，安吉拉，我们收到了一封来自内布拉斯加州贝尔维尤市凯瑟琳·P的信。

1822
01:19:04.100 --> 01:19:05.160
in Bellevue, Nebraska.
在内布拉斯加州的贝尔维尤。

1823
01:19:05.720 --> 01:19:07.400
And it really touched my heart.
它真的触动了我的心。

1824
01:19:07.500 --> 01:19:08.420
So I wanted to share.
所以我很想分享一下。

1825
01:19:08.620 --> 01:19:08.820
Okay.
好的。

1826
01:19:09.600 --> 01:19:10.560
Catherine said,
凯瑟琳说，

1827
01:19:10.560 --> 01:19:14.880
I wanted to tell you that this episode is incredibly meaningful to my family.
我想告诉你们，这一集对我的家庭意义非凡。

1828
01:19:15.140 --> 01:19:23.200
I started watching The Office on Netflix when I was pregnant with my oldest and just found out she would need heart surgery after she was born.
我怀大女儿时开始在网飞上看《办公室》，当时刚得知她出生后需要做心脏手术。

1829
01:19:23.800 --> 01:19:29.900
It was not only a lifesaver, but fast forward to my daughter born and waiting for surgery.
这不仅是我的救命稻草，后来女儿出生等待手术期间，

1830
01:19:30.160 --> 01:19:33.860
On her bad days, we would watch this episode specifically.
每当她状态不好时，我们就会专门看这一集。

1831
01:19:34.180 --> 01:19:39.860
My husband and entire family know that season seven, episode one is the lip dub.
我丈夫和全家人都知道第七季第一集是那个对口型表演。

1832
01:19:39.860 --> 01:19:45.120
My daughter would smile and light up for her favorite faces singing just for her.
我女儿看到她最喜欢的那些面孔为她唱歌时，会露出笑容，整个人都亮了起来。

1833
01:19:45.480 --> 01:19:48.360
She had surgery at four months old right before Christmas.
她在四个月大时，也就是圣诞节前夕做了手术。

1834
01:19:48.720 --> 01:19:52.260
The office kept us going during a very hard time for our little warrior.
在我们这位小战士最艰难的时刻，《办公室》支撑着我们走过来。

1835
01:19:52.700 --> 01:20:00.520
I took pictures of her laying in her swing, pleased as punch to be watching the lip dub for what had to have been the thousandth time.
我拍了她躺在摇椅里的照片，她看那个对口型表演看了不下上千遍，开心得不得了。

1836
01:20:01.200 --> 01:20:05.400
She is now a thriving and perfectly healthy eight-year-old.
她现在是一个健康活泼、八岁大的孩子了。

1837
01:20:05.480 --> 01:20:08.440
And we are forever grateful to the Scranton branch.
我们永远感激斯克兰顿分部。

1838
01:20:08.440 --> 01:20:09.560
P.S.
附言：

1839
01:20:09.640 --> 01:20:15.200
She had an opportunity to meet Kate Flannery several years ago, and she hasn't stopped talking about it since.
几年前她有机会见到了凯特·弗兰纳里，从那以后她就一直念叨着这件事。

1840
01:20:15.840 --> 01:20:17.820
That just made me tear up.
这让我热泪盈眶。

1841
01:20:18.080 --> 01:20:18.520
I know.
我也是。

1842
01:20:19.100 --> 01:20:22.720
Catherine, can we please send your daughter some office lady stuff?
凯瑟琳，我们能给你的女儿寄一些《办公室》周边吗？

1843
01:20:23.080 --> 01:20:24.840
We would love to send her something.
我们很想送她点什么。

1844
01:20:25.140 --> 01:20:26.960
Thank you so much for sharing that.
非常感谢你的分享。

1845
01:20:27.140 --> 01:20:30.540
I'm so glad that our show could be there for you and your family.
我很高兴我们的节目能陪伴你和你的家人。

1846
01:20:30.540 --> 01:20:36.220
Yeah, I love it that this episode specifically has a special place in your heart.
是啊，我很高兴这一集能在你心中占据特殊的位置。

1847
01:20:36.640 --> 01:20:37.960
Catherine, we're going to email you.
凯瑟琳，我们会给你发邮件的。

1848
01:20:38.160 --> 01:20:39.300
Be on the lookout for it.
请留意查收。

1849
01:20:39.760 --> 01:20:41.720
Well, you guys, that was nepotism.
好了，各位，以上就是《裙带关系》这一集的内容。

1850
01:20:41.920 --> 01:20:43.160
Sam is waving at us.
萨姆在向我们招手。

1851
01:20:43.300 --> 01:20:44.020
Sam, what do you got?
山姆，你查到了吗？

1852
01:20:44.140 --> 01:20:45.800
Did you find out about peeing in the pool?
你查到关于在泳池里尿尿的事了吗？

1853
01:20:45.900 --> 01:20:46.160
I did.
查到了。

1854
01:20:46.280 --> 01:20:48.400
If you look up at the TV, I believe you'll find your answer.
如果你抬头看电视，我想你会找到答案的。

1855
01:20:48.580 --> 01:20:49.600
Oh, all right.
哦，好吧。

1856
01:20:49.740 --> 01:20:50.300
Here it is.
就在这儿。

1857
01:20:50.400 --> 01:20:53.920
Does a swimming pool urine detecting dye actually exist?
真的存在能检测泳池尿液的染料吗？

1858
01:20:53.920 --> 01:20:58.000
It says, no such chemical is used.
上面说，并没有使用这种化学物质。

1859
01:20:58.420 --> 01:20:59.360
Doesn't exiSt.
根本不存在。

1860
01:20:59.620 --> 01:21:05.760
But 52% of people believe there is a chemical that when added to a pool will turn your urine a color.
但有52%的人相信，有一种化学物质加到泳池里后会让尿液变色。

1861
01:21:06.360 --> 01:21:06.920
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

1862
01:21:07.600 --> 01:21:11.380
We basically all believed our moms are people at the public pool.
我们基本上都相信了妈妈们在公共泳池里说的话。

1863
01:21:11.680 --> 01:21:19.240
It goes on to say, regardless, pools are not meant to be peed in because urine contains bacteria that you would not want to swim in.
上面还说，无论如何，泳池都不应该用来小便，因为尿液中含有你不希望在里面游泳时接触到的细菌。

1864
01:21:19.440 --> 01:21:21.420
Please do not pee in pools.
请不要在泳池里小便。

1865
01:21:21.840 --> 01:21:23.380
There you have it, guys.
真相就是这样，伙计们。

1866
01:21:23.380 --> 01:21:26.500
Yeah, it won't turn a color, but you shouldn't do it anyway.
没错，它不会变色，但你无论如何都不该那么做。

1867
